# Rank 1627 / CVE-2026-33699: pypdf's DictionaryObject.read_from_stream
# parsed dictionary key/value pairs in an unbounded while-True loop over
# the PDF byte stream, and its recovery policy converted every parsing
# error into warn-and-continue in non-strict mode. The recursion and
# self-reference guards existed -- PdfReader.get_object raises on a
# self-referencing indirect object, and deep nesting raises
# RecursionError -- but the parser swallows the errors in the same broad
# `except Exception` handler as ordinary malformed input, so the
# lenient parse re-read the same bytes forever: an infinite loop on a
# crafted PDF (CWE-835/CWE-400, denial of service; GHSA-87mj-5ggw-8qc3,
# fixed in 6.9.2). The fixed revision reclassifies RecursionError and
# LimitReachedError as hard errors that always propagate, in both the
# reader (the self-reference raise becomes LimitReachedError instead of
# PdfReadError) and the dictionary parser. The fixing commit da867f49 is the
# 6.9.2 release bump; the security fix it ships is 02b1345 (PR #3693),
# named in that release commit's own changelog -- no row correction correction
# reported, never applied.
#
# ATTENTION, lenient-recovery family (the unbounded-parse group with
# 1517, 1554, 1572, 1586 and 1612). The cycle guard fires and the limit
# errors are raised; what is missing is a judgement about which error
# classes a recovery handler must not absorb. No concept expresses it:
# NumericParserMissingProgressCheck (VYQL-DOS-029) is bound only in C
# for numeric parsers with a tmp == pos cursor guard,
# RecursiveObjectParentResolveWithoutCycleGuard covers a missing guard
# rather than a swallowed one, and the Python frontend emits no
# except-clause fact at all -- `vyql match` on a minimal repro of the
# function reports no source, no sink and no control. The only textual
# discriminator between the two revisions is the added
# `except (RecursionError, LimitReachedError)` clause, the fixing
# commit's own layout. A binding keyed on pypdf's logger_warning would
# detect this library rather than the weakness. Measured on the real
# checkout at 02b1345^ and 02b1345: 204 findings at both revisions,
# zero on pypdf/generic/_data_structures.py (the four on pypdf/_reader.py
# are ReDoS false positives on re.compile), identical rule tallies --
# no discrimination exists. No ENGINE-GAPS.md entry: no taint path is
# involved and no single construct is mishandled. No definition change
# shipped. Spec cve_rank1627 records the swallowed-limit form and the
# hard-error form, both asserting reject VYQL-DOS-029: when
# lenient-recovery vocabulary lands, the swallowed form must flip to
# expect.

test "rank1627: the lenient dictionary parser absorbs the limit errors"
  lang python
  file pypdf/generic/_data_structures.py
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class DictionaryObject(dict):
      @staticmethod
      def read_from_stream(stream, pdf, forced_encoding=None):
          data = {}
          while True:
              tok = read_non_whitespace(stream)
              if tok == b">":
                  stream.read(1)
                  break
              stream.seek(-1, 1)
              try:
                  try:
                      key = read_object(stream, pdf)
                      if isinstance(key, NullObject):
                          break
                  except PdfReadError as exc:
                      if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                          raise
                      logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                      continue
                  value = read_object(stream, pdf, forced_encoding)
              except Exception as exc:
                  if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                      raise PdfReadError(exc.__repr__())
                  logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                  retval = DictionaryObject()
                  retval.update(data)
                  return retval  # return partial data
              data[key] = value
          return DictionaryObject(data)
  ```

test "rank1627: recursion and limit errors are hard errors"
  lang python
  file pypdf/generic/_data_structures.py
  reject VYQL-DOS-029
  code
  ```
  class DictionaryObject(dict):
      @staticmethod
      def read_from_stream(stream, pdf, forced_encoding=None):
          data = {}
          while True:
              tok = read_non_whitespace(stream)
              if tok == b">":
                  stream.read(1)
                  break
              stream.seek(-1, 1)
              try:
                  try:
                      key = read_object(stream, pdf)
                      if isinstance(key, NullObject):
                          break
                  except PdfReadError as exc:
                      if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                          raise
                      logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                      continue
                  value = read_object(stream, pdf, forced_encoding)
              except (RecursionError, LimitReachedError) as exc:
                  raise PdfReadError(exc.__repr__())
              except Exception as exc:
                  if pdf is not None and pdf.strict:
                      raise PdfReadError(exc.__repr__())
                  logger_warning(exc.__repr__(), __name__)
                  retval = DictionaryObject()
                  retval.update(data)
                  return retval  # return partial data
              data[key] = value
          return DictionaryObject(data)
  ```
